    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass with a clean build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form for owner creation on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` (optional, normalized) and `addressLine2` (optional) to `OwnerFields`; these are inherited by the `Owner` response schema.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only owner passes request-body bean validation. `address` stays accepted as flat input and is now documented as the composed value on response.\n\n**Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields with `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns plus getters/setters. MapStruct maps them automatically in both directions.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- Replaced the single flat-address normalization with `applyAddressFields(...)`: when `addressLine1` is non-blank the structured form wins \u2014 `addressLine1` (and `addressLine2` when present) are normalized in place, and the flat `address` is set to the composed value (`normalized addressLine1` + a single space + `normalized addressLine2` only when line 2 is present). Otherwise the flat `address` is normalized as before.\n- Because the effective `address` is now the composed/structured value, the existing required-fields check (`address` + `city`) enforces the \"address in either form, plus city\" rule, and everything downstream that reads the address sees the structured value while backward-compatible minimal owners are still accepted.\n\n**Schema + seed data** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`, `db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`)\n- Added the two nullable columns at the end of the `owners` table and appended two `NULL`s to the positional seed inserts (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 and mysql) so column counts stay aligned.\n\nVerification: the three address checkpoints (Cp01 required-fields, Cp12 structured normalization, Cp44 compose/backward-compat) pass, and the full suite is green \u2014 **55 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
